{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.MvGenWronskian","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.MvGenWronskian","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.PDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.CommRing","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLinearEquiv","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Nondegenerate","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Degrees"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_iff_exists_mvGenWronskian_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_iff_exists_mvGenWronskian_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":633,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L633-L650","doc":"**Independence is exactly a non-vanishing generalized Wronskian**, in characteristic\nzero — the certificate Roth's lemma consumes, in both directions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_pow_five_six_constantCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_pow_five_six_constantCoeff","kind":"theorem","line":626,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L626-L631","doc":"...and that same Wronskian vanishes at the origin, so the argument used above could\nnever have produced it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_pow_five_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_pow_five_six","kind":"theorem","line":620,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L620-L624","doc":"Order-one operators already witness the independence of `x⁵, x⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_mvGenWronskian_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_mvGenWronskian_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":567,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L567-L604","doc":"**An independent family has a non-zero generalized Wronskian.**\n\nThe Wronskian is non-zero because it is non-zero **at the origin**. Independence gives a\nnon-singular coefficient minor at multi-indices `α`; realise each `α i` as a list of\nvariables to get the operator family; then `constantCoeff` is a ring hom, so it commutes\nwith the determinant, and the resulting scalar matrix is `diagonal c * coeffMatrix α f`.\n\n⚠ **Where characteristic zero enters, and why it cannot be avoided here.** The `c i` are\npositive integers — products of exponents thrown off by `coeff_pderiv`. Their product must\nbe non-zero *in `K`*, which is exactly `CharZero`. Over `𝔽ₚ` the same construction can\nproduce a genuinely zero determinant from an independent family, which is the multivariate\nface of the failure that makes the univariate converse false in characteristic `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_coeff_pderivList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_coeff_pderivList","kind":"theorem","line":539,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L539-L557","doc":"**Iterating `coeff_pderiv` along a list.**\n\n⚠ The constant depends only on `γ` and `l`, **never on `g`** — the quantifier order matters,\nbecause the whole point is to pull a single factor out of an entire matrix row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_multiIndexOf_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_multiIndexOf_eq","kind":"theorem","line":529,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L529-L537","doc":"**Every multi-index is realised by a list**, so an operator family can be built from any\nfamily of multi-indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_replicate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_replicate","kind":"theorem","line":523,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L523-L527","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_append","kind":"theorem","line":519,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L519-L521","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_cons","kind":"theorem","line":515,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L515-L517","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf_nil","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L513-L513","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.multiIndexOf","kind":"def","line":510,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L510-L511","doc":"The multi-index counting occurrences of each variable in a list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.map_det_pderivList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.map_det_pderivList","kind":"theorem","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L496-L508","doc":"**The determinant of derivatives commutes with a change of coefficient ring.**\n\nThis is what lets the arc's `ℚ`-valued separated Wronskian be recognised as the image of the\n*same* determinant formed over `ℤ` — and hence as a polynomial with integer coefficients,\nwhich is what §6's Gauss step needs of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.map_pderivList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.map_pderivList","kind":"theorem","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L486-L494","doc":"Iterated differentiation commutes with a change of coefficient ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_nil_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_nil_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L457-L475","doc":"**A bounded-order family can be degenerate**, and for `m ≥ 2` an obvious one always is:\ntake every operator list empty.  The order condition `|D i| ≤ i` holds (`0 ≤ i` for every\n`i`), the matrix has all rows equal to `f`, and the determinant vanishes.\n\n⚠ This is the record of the **tenth correction**.  A hypothesis of the form \"for *every*\nbounded-order family realising a separated representation of `P`, the Wronskians' indices are\nbounded\" is **unsatisfiable**: this family realises the same representation and its Wronskian\nis `0`, whose index is `⊤`.  Such a hypothesis has to be restricted to families whose\nWronskians do not vanish — which is exactly what `BoundedOrderWronskian` produces, and what\nthe argument was always using. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_of_mvGenWronskian_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_of_mvGenWronskian_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L438-L454","doc":"**A non-vanishing generalized Wronskian forces independence** — the contrapositive of\n`mvGenWronskian_eq_zero_of_dependent`.\n\n⚠ Worth having in this direction.  After the tenth correction, `hres` carries\n`mvGenWronskian Dx φ ≠ 0` and `mvGenWronskian Dy ψ ≠ 0`, and this says those hypotheses\nalready supply the independence that the factors' *degree* bounds need.  The repair for\ncorrection 10 turned out to hand over exactly what the next step was missing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.degreeOf_mvGenWronskian_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.degreeOf_mvGenWronskian_le","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L409-L436","doc":"**Degree bound for the generalized Wronskian:** `deg_{xᵢ} ≤ m · d` when every member of\nthe family has `deg_{xᵢ} ≤ d`.\n\n⚠ **This is what makes the independence certificate quantitative.** Roth's lemma does not\nmerely need *some* non-zero Wronskian — it needs one whose degree is controlled by the\ndegrees of the auxiliary polynomial, because the index estimate is measured against those\ndegrees. A certificate with no degree bound carries no arithmetic information. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.degreeOf_pderivList_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.degreeOf_pderivList_le","kind":"theorem","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L399-L407","doc":"Nor does any iterated partial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.degreeOf_pderiv_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.degreeOf_pderiv_le","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L387-L397","doc":"Differentiating never *raises* the degree in any variable.  Companion to\n`degreeOf_pderiv_lt`, which is the strict drop in the differentiated variable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.degreeOf_pderiv_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.degreeOf_pderiv_lt","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L366-L385","doc":"**Differentiating strictly drops the degree in that variable.**\n\nMathlib has the univariate `Polynomial.natDegree_derivative_lt`; the multivariate statement\nis a gap.  No characteristic hypothesis is needed: the vanishing that characteristic `p`\ncauses is exactly the hypothesis `pderiv j p ≠ 0` excludes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.eq_C_of_pderiv_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.eq_C_of_pderiv_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L344-L364","doc":"**A polynomial killed by every partial derivative is constant**, in characteristic zero.\n\nMathlib has the univariate `Polynomial.eq_C_of_derivative_eq_zero`; the multivariate\nstatement is a gap.  Characteristic zero is doing real work: over `𝔽ₚ` the polynomial `xᵖ`\nhas every partial derivative zero and is not constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_support_pderiv_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_support_pderiv_le","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L326-L342","doc":"**Differentiating does not enlarge the support:** `#supp(∂ⱼ g) ≤ #supp(g)`.\n\nThe support-size half of what `MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_le` needs, alongside the height half\nabove.  Same source, `coeff_pderiv`: it makes `γ ↦ γ + eⱼ` a map from `supp(∂ⱼ g)` into\n`supp(g)`, and that map is injective because addition cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderiv_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderiv_le","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L294-L324","doc":"**A height bound for a partial derivative:** `H(∂ⱼ g) ≤ degⱼ(g) · H(g)` over `ℤ`.\n\nImmediate from `coeff_pderiv`, which is an *identity*: the coefficient of `γ` in `∂ⱼ g` is\n`(γⱼ + 1)` times the coefficient of `γ + eⱼ` in `g`.  The factor `γⱼ + 1` is unbounded in\n`γ`, but it only ever multiplies a coefficient at exponent `γⱼ + 1` in the `j`-th variable —\nso beyond `degⱼ(g)` that coefficient is zero and the product vanishes.  The two cases in the\nproof are exactly those.\n\nThis grounds the height chain for the *entries* of a generalized Wronskian, whose matrix is\nbuilt from iterated `pderiv`s of the auxiliary polynomial.  ⚠ It does **not** yet bound the\ndeterminant — see `QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedHeight.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coeff_pderiv_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coeff_pderiv_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L280-L292","doc":"A monomial with a positive exponent is detected by the matching partial derivative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coeff_pderiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coeff_pderiv","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L252-L278","doc":"Differentiating shifts the coefficient index and multiplies by the exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_iff_exists_coeffMatrix_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_iff_exists_coeffMatrix_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L235-L240","doc":"**Independence is exactly a non-singular coefficient minor.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_of_coeffMatrix_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.linearIndependent_of_coeffMatrix_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L218-L233","doc":"A non-singular coefficient minor certifies independence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_coeffMatrix_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_coeffMatrix_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L155-L216","doc":"**An independent family has a non-singular coefficient minor.**\n\nInduction on `m`, by cofactor expansion along the new row. If *every* extension of the\ninductive minor were singular, the cofactors along that row would give a fixed linear\nrelation `∑ⱼ cⱼ · coeff β (fⱼ) = 0` holding at **every** multi-index `β` — and a relation\nholding at every coefficient is a relation between the polynomials themselves. The cofactor\nin the last column is the inductive minor, so `c` is not the zero vector, contradicting\nindependence.\n\n⚠ The cofactors must not depend on `β`, which is why the expansion is along the *last* row:\ndeleting it removes every entry `β` occurs in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coeffMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coeffMatrix","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L150-L153","doc":"The matrix of coefficients of `f` at the multi-indices `α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_one_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_one_X","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L125-L135","doc":"⚠ **Non-vacuity.**  `mvGenWronskian_eq_zero_of_dependent` is used through its\ncontrapositive, which certifies nothing if every generalized Wronskian vanishes\nidentically.  It does not: against the operators `(id, ∂/∂x₀)` the family `(1, x₀)` gives\nthe identity matrix.\n\nThis also exhibits why `D` is *chosen* rather than canonical — with `D = (id, id)` the\nmatrix has two equal rows and the determinant vanishes for every family, dependent or not,\nso a \"for all `D`\" independence certificate would be empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_eq_zero_of_dependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian_eq_zero_of_dependent","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L98-L123","doc":"**A constant linear dependence kills every generalized Wronskian.**\n\nThe direction Roth's lemma consumes, via its contrapositive: if *some* generalized\nWronskian is non-zero, the family is linearly independent over the constants.\n\nThe proof is the same one the univariate file uses — the constant vector sits in the kernel\nof the matrix, so the determinant vanishes — and it works verbatim because\n`pderivList_sum_C_mul` is all that was ever needed of the derivative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvGenWronskian","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L92-L96","doc":"The **generalized Wronskian** in several variables, against a chosen family of `m`\ndifferential operators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvWronskianMatrix_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvWronskianMatrix_apply","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mvWronskianMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mvWronskianMatrix","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L82-L86","doc":"The **generalized Wronskian matrix** in several variables: entry `(i, j)` is the `i`-th\ndifferential operator applied to `f j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.pderivList_sum_C_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.pderivList_sum_C_mul","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L71-L80","doc":"A differential operator carries a constant-coefficient combination through.\n\nThis is the only property of the operators the Wronskian argument uses — in particular it\nnever needs them to commute, which is why no ordering condition appears on `D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.pderivList_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.pderivList_cons","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L67-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.pderivList_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.pderivList_nil","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L64-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.pderivList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.pderivList","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/MvGenWronskian.lean#L59-L62","doc":"Iterated partial derivative along a list of variables, **as a linear map** — which is\nwhat makes the linearity the Wronskian argument needs free rather than proved. ","signatureChunk":0}]}